scopecontent.p:
Attempts to discourage Kemble
from performing at the Theatre Royal,
Norwich.

Thanks recipient for his letter;
replies that Mr. Jennings is now much
better.

Describes interview with Miss
Clement for teaching post at Middlesex;
thanks him for a copy of his book.

Reply to M. Eden's letter of Nov 4;
treats finances of Mr. [Fitz ...]
and discusses a trip to the Hague.

Describes the anguish of a
mutual friend leading to his death;
P. Forster.

Concerns his research into
Elizabethan botany and gardening;
other antiquarian subjects;
Robert Cecil, 1st earl of Salisbury.

Also signed by John Motteux;
concerns an arbitration between
Mr. Droz and Mr. Boulton.

Commendation on his installation
as Provost of Eton College;
in Latin and Greek.

Preface to a history of Cambria;
a second MS is thought not to be from
the time of James I.

Talks of his Mediterranean trip
and meeting Heinrich Schliemann;
in French.

Promise to pay enclosed; comments
on portrait to be hung in a gallery;
thanks for hospitality in Rome;
in Italian.

List of plaster casts and prices;
arrival of box and astrology chart
from Paris; in Italian.

Shipping Hoare's paintings to London;
plans to take a putto of his design
to Sweden.

Letters to brother-in-law
congratulating him on safe arrival
in Ireland; family news; Lord Hyde's
return from campaign in Flanders;
King and Parliament; Lord Cassell;
Duncombe; Lady Arlington, etc.

About his nephew who has gone to sea;
wants Spottiswoode to pay the Customs
House in his absence.

Desires copies of 2 tracts for
Highfield Society's 5th anniversary;
discusses affairs of the society.

