[Letters Relating to the Paddle Steamer 
                           Rotterdam
                        ]

scopecontent.p:
1) ALS from James Watt to Lt. Richard
Bastard; Norfolk Hotel, 1822 Jun 9;
2) Letter copy of ALS from Bastard
to the Admiralty Office; 2 Clifford's
Inn, 1822 Jun 6;
3) LS from Sir John Barrow to Bastard;
Admiralty Office, 1822 Jul 9;
4) ALS (copy) from Money Wigram to
the Admiralty Office; Blackwall
Yard, 1822 Jul 24;
5) LS from J. W. Croker to Wigram;
Admiralty Office, 1822 Aug 2.
With: cover.
All concern the unsuccessful efforts
to obtain Admiralty permission for
Bastard to command the paddle steamer Rotterdam. Acc.: 04.12.3
